6 --> 27Complexity Analysis of a Hash Table:For lookup, insertion, and deletion operations, hash tables have an average-case time complexity of O(1). Yet, these operations may, in the worst case, require O(n) time, where n is the number of elements in the table.Applications of Hash Table:Hash tables are frequently used for indexing and searching massive volumes of data. A search engine might use a hash table to store the web pages that it has indexed.Data is usually cached in memory via hash tables, enabling rapid access to frequently used information. Hash functions are frequently used in cryptography to create digital signatures, validate data, and guarantee data integrity.Hash tables can be used for implementing database indexes, enabling fast access to data based on key values.
